   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight lunge to g4 looks intimidating but there's nothing to fear — simply castle. If it grabs on f2 and the bishop recaptures, the trade leaves two pieces for a rook and pawn, and in the middlegame the rooks stay stuck in their corners while the two minor pieces run the board.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 104,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np4/2b1p3/4P1n1/2N2NP1/PPPP1PBP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 128,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np4/2b1p3/4P1n1/2N2NPP/PPPP1PB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "h3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The h-pawn move chases the knight and forces a decision. There's no real hurry — a quiet pawn move would also do — but making the opponent commit costs nothing."
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 135,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np3n/2b1p3/4P3/2N2NPP/PPPP1PB1/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Nh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The retreat to h6 is an awkward square, and it telegraphs the plan — a quick f5 push, which is close to suicidal with the king still stuck in the centre."
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 162,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np3n/2b1p3/4P3/2NP1NPP/PPP2PB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "d3"
   ],
   "spoken": "So there's no need to change course — just play the standard d3, completing development while quietly setting up the positional threat of capturing on h6. Playing the system's own moves is exactly the appeal of it.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 168,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/ppp2ppp/2np3n/2b1p3/4P3/2NP1NPP/PPP2PB1/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 9",
   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 192,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/ppp2ppp/2np3B/2b1p3/4P3/2NP1NPP/PPP2PB1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Bxh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "A subtlety about that capture on h6: it's strong not because it doubles the pawns — pawn structure is routinely overrated — but because the king has castled onto that very wing. Had the opponent kept the king elsewhere, ruining the structure would be far less tempting."
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 197,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np3n/2b1p3/4P3/2NP1NPP/PPP2PB1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 8",
