   "spoken": "Why is this near-winning when the material is level — a rook and pawn balancing the two pieces? Because once the centre opens, it's effectively two extra minor pieces: the rooks are marooned out of the game while the knights and bishop leap into dominant central posts. Mobilised force, not the material count, is what decides it.",
